course: dictionary
lesson: 14347
title: Offensiveness and how it hurts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words and actions are rude or hurtful, and we call that quality offensiveness. It is a noun, so it names a thing: how rude or hurtful something is. Look at the words around it for clues. «The offensiveness of his joke about her accent made the whole class go quiet.» The joke hurt someone, so the sentence shows that offensiveness means hurtfulness.
explain: Offensiveness can also describe something very unpleasant to the senses, like a smell. «The offensiveness of the rotting rubbish filled the whole street.» Nobody is being insulted here. The smell is so nasty that it is hard to bear, so the context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: Quick check: swap in «how rude or hurtful» and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: Offensiveness means the quality of being rude or hurtful.
fact: «Offensive» is the adjective, and offensiveness is the noun made from it.
fact: «The offensiveness of the comment» means how much the comment hurts or insults people.
fact: Offensiveness can also mean a very unpleasant smell or taste, as in «the offensiveness of the smell».
fact: Online, a joke or comment with high offensiveness can upset people, so think before you post.
exercise: «The offensiveness of his joke about her accent made the whole class go quiet.» What does offensiveness mean here? | *How hurtful or rude the joke was | How loudly he told it | How funny the joke was | How long the joke lasted
exercise: Mia says offensiveness is a happy feeling you get with friends. What is the right meaning? | *Being rude or hurtful to people | A type of tasty food | Feeling very happy with friends | Being very tired after school
exercise: Find the adjective in this sentence, the word that comes from the same family as offensiveness: «The comment was offensive to everyone in the room.» | everyone | comment | *offensive | room
test: «The offensiveness of the rotting rubbish filled the whole street.» Here offensiveness means | A kind, gentle feeling | A loud song | *A very nasty, unpleasant smell | A sunny day
test: Ben says, «Think about the offensiveness of your message before you send it.» What should Ben think about? | What colour the screen is | Whether it will rain tomorrow | How many letters his message has | *Whether his message could hurt or insult someone
exam: In «The offensiveness of the film's language meant it was rated for older viewers», what is offensiveness closest to? | *Rudeness or hurtfulness | Happiness | Brightness | Length
